      "description": "Dean College\nJob Posting: Campus Police Sergeant (Part-Time) Dean College \n\tJob Posting: Campus Police Sergeant (Part-Time) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Campus Police Sergeant (Part-Time) Category: Administration/Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Campus Police & Safety Locations: Franklin, MA Posted: Mar 18, 2026 Closes: Open Until Filled Type: Part-Time Fiscal Year Position ID: 198249 Share About Dean College: Dean College is a private, residential New England college grounded in a culture and tradition that all students deserve the opportunity to discover and exceed their greatest aspirations. A personal and transformative community since 1865, Dean tirelessly inspires our students to unimagined heights through personalized support and integrated delivery of academic, co-curricular, and experiential learning. Our graduates are lifelong learners who thrive in their careers, embrace social responsibility, and demonstrate leadership. Recognized as a Top Regional College by U.S. News & World Report for fifteenth consecutive years and named a College of Distinction for eleven consecutive years, Dean serves more than 1,000 full-time students and offers over 50 academic programs and specializations, as well as a robust schedule of continuing studies and certificate programs throughout the year. Dean College is perfectly situated in Franklin, Massachusetts, which is conveniently located between Boston and Providence, Rhode Island, and is accessible to Boston by commuter rail. The Dean College/Franklin rail station is only a five-minute walk from campus. Approximately 90 percent of the College's student population lives on campus and Dean provides a supportive academic environment that thrives on hands-on engagement and exceptional teaching. This community-wide commitment of always going the extra mile for students is known as The Dean Difference. Outside of the classroom, students participate in 16 athletic teams and more than 40 on-campus groups and organizations. Ninety-six percent of our bachelor's degree students are employed or enrolled in graduate school within 12 months of graduation. Alumni are hard at work in top-ranked graduate programs and are employed by organizations such as Universal Studios, Dell Technologies, Liberty Mutual, Kraft Sports + Entertainment, the Boston Ballet, and more. What is The Dean Difference? The Dean Difference isn't any one thing. It's not a program or a professor. It's not a single class or a club. It's the way our academic support networks and community overlap, interweave, and magnify each other. Our difference unites us. It's our secret formula. It's the nucleus around which we orbit. It isn't one thing, it's everything. Job Description: The Campus Police Sergeant supervises shift officers and manages daily operations to ensure the effective delivery of campus safety and police services. This role is dedicated to protecting Dean College property and supporting the safety and well-being of the campus community, while upholding the department's mission to maintain a secure and welcoming environment. Position responsibilities include: Supervise shift officers, ensuring operational effectiveness, adherence to policies, and high standards of professional conduct. Patrol campus buildings and grounds to deter crime, vandalism, theft, and other violations of law or college policies. Respond to, investigate, and document incidents, policy violations, and criminal activity. Refer cases to the Office of Community Standards when appropriate, investigate accidents, and provide guidance and information to the campus community. Foster positive relationships between the police department and the campus community through proactive engagement, education, and daily interactions. Review and approve reports, citations, and other required administrative documentation. Oversee officer scheduling, performance evaluations, coaching, and ongoing training initiatives. Develop and implement educational programs and safety training tailored to campus needs and emerging safety trends. Provide additional security at college-sponsored events as required. Deliver transportation and escort services, including walking or vehicle safety escorts, and non-emergency medical transports to local facilities. Perform other duties as assigned to support the safety and security mission of the college. Requirements: Qualifications and Requirements Associate's degree in criminal justice or a related field required; bachelor's degree preferred. 5-7 years of sworn law enforcement experience, preferably in campus or community-oriented policing. Massachusetts POST certification (or eligibility) and MPTC full-time police academy certification. Valid, unrestricted driver's license with an acceptable driving record. Valid Massachusetts License to Carry Firearms (Large Capacity) in accordance with MGL Chapter 140, Section 131. Successful completion of a comprehensive background investigation, medical exam, and psychological evaluation. Flexibility to work varied shifts, including nights, weekends, holidays, and during campus emergencies and events. Knowledge and Skills Strong knowledge of criminal law, investigative procedures, campus policing practices, CJIS, and Clery Act compliance. Demonstrated leadership, supervisory, mentoring, and team-building experience. Experience supervising and evaluating sworn and civilian personnel. Excellent interpersonal, communication, and conflict resolution skills, particularly in a campus environment. Professional and effective interaction with students, faculty, staff, and the public. Proven judgment in handling sensitive situations with discretion and professionalism. Sound decision-making in emergency and high-pressure situations. Proficiency in report writing and maintaining detailed, accurate records. Collaborative approach to working with college administration, student affairs, and community partners. Experience with staffing, scheduling, and shift management. Additional Information: Dean College is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate against applicants or employees on the basis of race, color, religion, religious creed, national or ethnic origin, ancestry, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, or any other status protected by applicable law. This commitment applies to all employment practices, including recruitment, hiring, promotion, compensation, benefits, professional development, continuation of employment, and other terms and conditions of employment. The College prohibits discrimination, harassment, and retaliation in violation of applicable law or College policy. Dean College is committed to maintaining a welcoming and respectful workplace and to providing equal opportunity to all qualified applicants and employees. Application Instructions: Please submit your Resume/CV, Cover Letter, all unofficial transcripts; and contact information of three references. (PLEASE NOTE: Applications that are incomplete will not be considered). Note: After submitting your resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your Cover Letter and any additional documents. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your Dean College Careers Account to check your completed application or upload additional documents. URL: www.dean.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Dean College 99 Main Street, Franklin MA 02038"
    },
    "https://dean.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=197200": {
      "title": "Dean College \n\tJob Posting: Campus Safety Officer (Full-Time/Part-Time, Overnight)",
      "description": "Dean College\nJob Posting: Campus Safety Officer (Full-Time/Part-Time, Overnight) Dean College \n\tJob Posting: Campus Safety Officer (Full-Time/Part-Time, Overnight) Title Human Resources Subscribe to Email Alerts Returning Applicant Login Previous Next Careers > Search Jobs > Search Results > Job Details Campus Safety Officer (Full-Time/Part-Time, Overnight) Category: Administration/Staff Subscribe: New Job Alerts RSS Job Feed Department: Campus Police & Safety Locations: Franklin, MA Posted: Feb 10, 2026 Closes: Oct 2, 2026 - 11:59 PM EDT Type: Full-Time Fiscal Year Position ID: 197200 Share About Dean College: Dean College is a private, residential New England college grounded in a culture and tradition that all students deserve the opportunity to discover and exceed their greatest aspirations. A personal and transformative community since 1865, Dean tirelessly inspires our students to unimagined heights through personalized support and integrated delivery of academic, co-curricular, and experiential learning. Our graduates are lifelong learners who thrive in their careers, embrace social responsibility, and demonstrate leadership. Recognized as a Top Regional College by U.S. News & World Report for thirteen consecutive years and named a College of Distinction for nine consecutive years, Dean serves approximately 1,200 full-time students and 400 part-time students and offers more than 50 combined bachelor's and associate degree programs and specializations, as well as a robust schedule of continuing studies and certificate programs throughout the year. Dean College is perfectly situated in Franklin, Massachusetts, which is conveniently located between Boston and Providence, Rhode Island, and is accessible to Boston by commuter rail. The Dean College/Franklin rail station is only a five-minute walk from campus. Approximately 90 percent of the College's student population lives on campus and Dean provides a supportive academic environment that thrives on hands-on engagement and exceptional teaching. This community-wide commitment of always going the extra mile for students is known as The Dean Difference. Outside of the classroom, students participate in 16 athletic teams and more than 40 on-campus groups and organizations. Ninety-six percent of our bachelor's degree students are employed or enrolled in graduate school within 12 months of graduation. Alumni are hard at work in top-ranked graduate programs and are employed by organizations such as Universal Studios, Dell Technologies, Liberty Mutual, Kraft Sports + Entertainment, the Boston Ballet, and more. What is The Dean Difference ? The Dean Difference isn't any one thing. It's not a program or a professor. It's not a single class or a club. It's the way our academic support networks and community overlap, interweave, and magnify each other. Our difference unites us. It's our secret formula. It's the nucleus around which we orbit. It isn't one thing, it's everything. Job Description: The Campus Safety Officer is responsible for maintaining a safe and secure environment for students, faculty, staff, and visitors of the College. This role involves proactive patrol of campus facilities and grounds, responding to calls for service, enforcing College policies, and supporting compliance with applicable laws and regulations. The Campus Safety Officer serves as a visible presence on campus, provides assistance and information to the campus community, supports educational safety initiatives, and collaborates with local and sworn law enforcement when necessary. The position also includes supervisory responsibilities for student employees and a strong commitment to community-oriented campus safety. Full-time and part-time positions are available. The starting hourly rate ranges from $22.50-$25.00, depending on qualifications and experience. A $1.00 per hour shift differential is provided for overnight shifts. Full-time employees work a 4 days on / 2 days off shift schedule. Position responsibilities include: Conduct regular patrols of campus buildings and grounds to deter criminal activity, prevent theft and vandalism, and ensure compliance with college policies. Respond promptly to calls for service; investigate, document, and report incidents involving violations of the College's Code of Conduct and applicable state laws. Refer incidents to the Office of Student Conduct & Community Standards for follow-up and disciplinary action when appropriate; provide guidance and information to members of the campus community. Assist with campus safety education, training, and outreach programs based on identified needs and emerging trends. Provide transportation services, including campus safety escorts (on foot or by vehicle), non-emergency medical transports to local medical facilities, and other assigned transportation duties. Support sworn law enforcement personnel during assigned shifts, as needed. Supervise, support, and assist student employees participating in work-study or internship assignments within Campus Police & Safety. Identify and report potential safety concerns or problematic issues to the direct supervisor in a timely and professional manner. Perform additional duties as assigned to support and enhance the overall safety and security of the campus. Requirements: Associate's degree in criminal justice or a related field is preferred. Must possess and maintain a valid, unrestricted driver's license and meet the College's insurability requirements as determined by Dean College Risk Management. Demonstrated strong interpersonal and human relations skills, with the ability to remain calm and effective in high-stress or emergency situations. Ability to assess emergency and non-emergency situations, exercise sound judgment, and implement appropriate and effective responses. Additional Information: Dean College is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate against applicants or employees on the basis of race, color, religion, religious creed, national or ethnic origin, ancestry, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, or any other status protected by applicable law. This commitment applies to all employment practices, including recruitment, hiring, promotion, compensation, benefits, professional development, continuation of employment, and other terms and conditions of employment. The College prohibits discrimination, harassment, and retaliation in violation of applicable law or College policy. Dean College is committed to maintaining a welcoming and respectful workplace and to providing equal opportunity to all qualified applicants and employees. Application Instructions: Please submit your Resume/CV, Cover Letter, all unofficial transcripts; and contact information of three references. (PLEASE NOTE: Applications that are incomplete will not be considered). Note: After submitting your resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your Cover Letter and any additional documents. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your Dean College Careers Account to check your completed application or upload additional documents. URL: www.dean.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Dean College 99 Main Street, Franklin MA 02038"
    },
    "https://dean.interviewexchange.com/jobofferdetails.jsp?JOBID=204048": {
      "title": "Dean College \n\tJob Posting: Resident Director",
