students participate in 16 athletic teams and more than 40 on-campus groups and organizations. Ninety-six percent of our bachelor's degree students are employed or enrolled in graduate school within 12 months of graduation. Alumni are hard at work in top-ranked graduate programs and are employed by organizations such as Universal Studios, Dell Technologies, Liberty Mutual, Kraft Sports + Entertainment, the Boston Ballet, and more. What is The Dean Difference? The Dean Difference isn't any one thing. It's not a program or a professor. It's not a single class or a club. It's the way our academic support networks and community overlap, interweave, and magnify each other. Our difference unites us. It's our secret formula. It's the nucleus around which we orbit. It isn't one thing, it's everything. Job Description: The Resident Director is a key member of the Office of Residence Life who supports student development and success by fostering a welcoming, inclusive, and engaging residential community at Dean College. This role oversees the day-to-day operations of assigned residence halls, supervises and mentors Resident Assistants, and partners with students to create a positive living and learning environment. The Resident Director also contributes to the broader mission of Residence Life through additional responsibilities as assigned. The anticipated additional responsibility for this role is assisting with housing operations management for the department of Residence Life. This is a full-time, 12-month, exempt position with a fixed, non-negotiable annual salary of $43,888. The position includes a live-in requirement, with the Resident Director receiving an unfurnished campus apartment (utilities included) within a residence hall and a meal plan when the dining center is open. In addition, the College offers a comprehensive benefits package that includes health insurance, retirement contributions, and generous paid time off. Position responsibilities include: Serve as the primary contact and manage an overall residential area of 200-300 upper-class students. Oversee all residential operations of assigned halls including opening and closing, occupancy management, room condition reports and inspections, damage billing, and building security. Demonstrates strong communication amongst residents, campus partners, and family outreach to ensure student success and belonging. Utilizes cultural humility and equity-mindedness in the creation and implementation of residential education, specialized programs, events, and living learning communities for the residential community. Process applications, manage room or apartment inventory, and coordinate move-in and move-out schedules using eRezlife housing software. Directly supervise student staff members (Resident Assistants); providing regular 1:1s and ongoing training, support, and evaluation. Respond to student behavior that is in violation of community standards, and/or impacts other residents; act as a mediator to roommate and/or intergroup conflict when needed. Participate in the Resident Director on-call rotation by responding to after-hour and weekend emergencies; provides counsel and crisis intervention when needed. Act as a hearing officer when deemed necessary. Other duties as assigned and/or required. Managerial and Supervisory Responsibilities: Provide direct supervision and leadership to residential student staff. Requirements: Bachelor's degree required, master's degree preferred. Previous experience in residence life is preferred. Previous experience using eRezLife or similar software. Demonstrated knowledge of best practices in managing housing assignments, occupancy management, and other residential logistics. Knowledge of relevant, global issues affecting college students. Demonstrated ability to work with and create community amongst a diverse student body and colleagues that facilitates positive outcomes, attested inclusivity, and effective communication strategies. Proven ability to identify issues, recognize obstacles, and resolve a wide range of problems commonly encountered in the Office of Residence Life. Exceptional skills in problem-solving, organization, intervention, and crisis management. Additional Information: Dean College is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate against applicants or employees on the basis of race, color, religion, religious creed, national or ethnic origin, ancestry, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, or any other status protected by applicable law. This commitment applies to all employment practices, including recruitment, hiring, promotion, compensation, benefits, professional development, continuation of employment, and other terms and conditions of employment. The College prohibits discrimination, harassment, and retaliation in violation of applicable law or College policy. Dean College is committed to maintaining a welcoming and respectful workplace and to providing equal opportunity to all qualified applicants and employees. Application Instructions: Please submit your Resume/CV, Cover Letter, all unofficial transcripts; and contact information of three references. (PLEASE NOTE: Applications that are incomplete will not be considered). Note: After submitting your resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your Cover Letter and any additional documents. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your Dean College Careers Account to check your completed application or upload additional documents. URL: www.dean.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Dean College 99 Main Street, Franklin MA 02038"
