Dean Difference. Outside of the classroom, students participate in 16 athletic teams and more than 40 on-campus groups and organizations. Ninety-six percent of our bachelor's degree students are employed or enrolled in graduate school within 12 months of graduation. Alumni are hard at work in top-ranked graduate programs and are employed by organizations such as Universal Studios, Dell Technologies, Liberty Mutual, Kraft Sports + Entertainment, the Boston Ballet, and more. What is The Dean Difference? The Dean Difference isn't any one thing. It's not a program or a professor. It's not a single class or a club. It's the way our academic support networks and community overlap, interweave, and magnify each other. Our difference unites us. It's our secret formula. It's the nucleus around which we orbit. It isn't one thing, it's everything. Job Description: The Assistant Coach for the Football team assists the head coach with program management, including practice planning, recruitment, player development, and competition strategy implementation. The Assistant Coach will support all aspects of the NCAA Division III Football program at Dean College, ensuring compliance with NCAA, Massachusetts State Collegiate Athletic Conference, and Dean College standards, rules, and regulations. This is a 10-month, part-time, non-exempt position with a fixed, non-negotiable rate of $15.00 per hour. Position responsibilities include: Assist in the implementation of the sport training and instructional program under the direction of the head coach by providing sport skill instruction, assisting in the conduct of practice sessions, performing game-related duties, and motivating players to give their best efforts. Recruit prospective student-athletes effectively as assigned by and under the direction of the head coach. Serve as a liaison with academic support personnel in support of players' academic efforts. Act as a liaison with the athletic training and strength and conditioning staff to support the conditioning and rehabilitation of players. Aid with administrative tasks, including fundraising and community service activities. Additional responsibility as assigned or required. Requirements: Bachelor's degree, required. Master's degree and/or coaching certification, preferred. Playing experience at the collegiate level and 3-5 years of experience as an assistant coach, preferred. Additional Information: Dean College is committed to equal employment opportunity and does not discriminate against applicants or employees on the basis of race, color, religion, religious creed, national or ethnic origin, ancestry, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, pregnancy or pregnancy-related condition, age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, marital status, or any other status protected by applicable law. This commitment applies to all employment practices, including recruitment, hiring, promotion, compensation, benefits, professional development, continuation of employment, and other terms and conditions of employment. The College prohibits discrimination, harassment, and retaliation in violation of applicable law or College policy. Dean College is committed to maintaining a welcoming and respectful workplace and to providing equal opportunity to all qualified applicants and employees. Application Instructions: Please submit your Resume/CV, Cover Letter, all unofficial transcripts; and contact information of three references. (PLEASE NOTE: Applications that are incomplete will not be considered). Note: After submitting your resume/CV, the subsequent page gives you instructions that enable you to upload your Cover Letter and any additional documents. See the FAQ for using our online system. Please contact us if you need assistance applying through this website. Returning Applicants - Login to your Dean College Careers Account to check your completed application or upload additional documents. URL: www.dean.edu Frequently Asked Questions (FAQs) Powered by Hide Main Navigation Dean College 99 Main Street, Franklin MA 02038"
